<% title "Fee Revenues" %>

<%# FUIME-DISABLED: `FeeRevenue` is the HQ side of HCB's fiscal-sponsorship fee sweep.

    BankFeeService::Weekly rolls that week's BankFees into one FeeRevenue and books it
    to `EventMappingEngine::EventIds::HACK_CLUB_BANK` (id 636) — see FeeRevenue#event.
    That is Hack Club's own org, not Ninth Street Labs, and settling it runs through
    Column, which Fuime does not have.

    Fuime's real revenue under merchant-of-record is the platform fee line
    Fuime::PaymentWebhookHandler#record_platform_fee writes at checkout, plus the
    payout side in Fuime::PayoutBatch. Neither passes through this model.

    View, controller action and model stay on disk (Rule 2); the admin route is removed,
    so this is unreachable by URL. Nothing can create a FeeRevenue under MoR.

    ⚠️ L8: the "Uncharged Fee Balance" below is NOT what Fuime charges. It is
    Event#fee_balance_v2_cents, a pure `amount × revenue_fee` accrual with NO 50c
    floor, whereas the real charge is Event#fuime_fee_cents_on => max(5%, 50c).
    It is also not money owed: under MoR the fee was already taken at checkout, and
    FeeEngine::Create waives the accrual for every Fuime-keyed transaction. A non-zero
    figure here means something built a fee accrual outside the MoR path — seeded /
    playground ventures (Fuime::Playground runs on Event::Plan::Free) or an
    invoice/manual line — and should be investigated, not collected. The number is
    left as the code computes it rather than "corrected" here; fixing it means fixing
    the accrual, not the view. %>
<div class="mb3">
  <h3>Uncharged Fee Balance: <%= render_money @total_pending_fees %></h3>

  <details>
    <summary>View breakdown by business (<%= @uncharged_fees_events.count %> businesses)</summary>

    <table class="mt2">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Business</th>
          <th>Fee Balance</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <% @uncharged_fees_events.each do |item| %>
          <tr>
            <td><%= link_to item[:event].name, event_path(item[:event]) %></td>
            <td><%= render_money item[:balance] %></td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </details>
</div>

<hr class="mb3">

<div class="flex items-center mb2 flex-col sm:flex-row">
  <div class="flex-grow">
    <%= page_entries_info @fee_revenues, entry_name: "fee revenues" %>
  </div>
  <%= paginate @fee_revenues %>
</div>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>ID</th>
      <th>Created</th>
      <th>Status</th>
      <th>Start Date</th>
      <th>End Date</th>
      <th>Amount</th>
      <th>Fuime Code</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <% @fee_revenues.each do |fee_revenue| %>
      <tr>
        <td><%= fee_revenue.id %></td>
        <td><%= fee_revenue.created_at.strftime("%Y-%m-%d") %></td>
        <td><%= fee_revenue.aasm_state %></td>
        <td><%= fee_revenue.start&.strftime("%Y-%m-%d") %></td>
        <td><%= fee_revenue.end&.strftime("%Y-%m-%d") %></td>
        <td><%= render_money_amount(fee_revenue.amount_cents) %></td>
        <td><%= link_to fee_revenue.hcb_code, hcb_code_path(fee_revenue.hcb_code) %></td>
      </tr>
    <% end %>
  </tbody>
</table>

<%= paginate @fee_revenues %>
